From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:51:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep bionic pthread cleanup handlers on every guest

__pthread_cleanup_push and __pthread_cleanup_pop only link a guest
__pthread_cleanup_t into the calling thread's pthread_internal_t
cleanup_stack. Where the emulator gives each guest thread a bionic
thread record of the guest's own layout, bionic's definitions work
as they are, and the emulator's thread exit walks the same
cleanup_stack. The stubs would hand the host a guest record it
cannot link into its own (glibc) thread, and glibc has no
__pthread_cleanup_push. Drop the two stubs from the arm, arm64 and
x86_64 lists so bionic's (weak for native bridge) definitions
define them.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NBS forwards to a host bionic whose thread record is the guest's]
Patch-Reason: the stub list is compiled into the guest libc; nothing outside the source removes a stub definition
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 android_api/libc/stubs_arm.cpp    | 4 ----
 android_api/libc/stubs_arm64.cpp  | 4 ----
 android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp | 4 ----
 3 files changed, 12 deletions(-)

